WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.891
Picture one round of copying as a

00:00:01.938 --> 00:00:02.495
timeline.

00:00:03.029 --> 00:00:06.327
While copying happens, DNA polymerase proofreads.

00:00:06.721 --> 00:00:08.649
It fixes a wrong base right away.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:10.657
Now copying is done.

00:00:11.284 --> 00:00:13.768
After that, mismatch repair proteins scan the

00:00:13.815 --> 00:00:14.744
finished DNA.

00:00:15.278 --> 00:00:17.136
They fix wrong bases they find.

00:00:17.588 --> 00:00:19.341
It's like fixing typos as you type,

00:00:19.562 --> 00:00:21.095
then rereading the essay after.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.917
Proofreading is during.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.891
Mismatch repair is after.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.946
Now try the question again.
